WEBVTT

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:15.740
Starting today, this is where you will live.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:23.580
He's here.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:01:00.430
No matter how far apart we 
are, we can't be stopped

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:05.430
That's deeply engraved into us

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:13.920
So don't be afraid of getting hurt

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:19.930
Breakthrough even further

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:25.440
While carrying you beliefs in your heart

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:32.590
There's always only one truth

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:36.480
So feel the voice of your heart

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:41.270
With your unwavering emotions

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:47.370
Seize the signs of tomorrow

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:22.680
Feelings Toward the CardsRigged 
Lightning Death Match

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:27.760
Get in.  This is your room.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.690
So they put you in here.

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:35.040
That makes me happy.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:40.970
You can take the top bunk, even though new 
people are normally supposed to take the lower bunk.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:43.560
Things like that don't bother me.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:46.370
Hey you…

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:48.390
Sheesh.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:10.320
Are you a Signer?

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.230
Signer?

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:16.490
According to the legend of the people of 
the stars, the Crimson Dragon is their god.

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:21.960
The people who summon it have the mark 
of the dragon and are known as Signers.

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:29.370
I just wanted to talk about the relationship 
between Neo Domino City and Satellite.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:35.320
I'm willing to sacrifice one side 
to ensure the survival of the other.

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:40.430
Hey you.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:41.720
What is it?

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:47.170
You're incredible.  You beat Himuro.

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:50.400
My name is Aoyama.  Nice to meet you.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:56.180
I also watched that duel.  
Your name is Yusei, right?

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:58.180
Sorry, but can you be quiet?

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:00.330
I see.

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:01.390
Bro.

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:02.900
Bro.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:06.370
Grandpa.

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:12.710
Himuro…

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:16.760
Yusei, you were also transferred here?

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:20.240
Why is this happening to me?

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:23.580
This area is for long-term detainees.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:28.560
I was supposed to be transferred to 
community service so that I can leave here quickly.

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:30.620
Same with me.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.710
Bro, do you have any idea why?

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:36.790
We really can't escape from here?

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:37.890
Yeah.

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:42.060
Since we were transferred here, we're 
guaranteed to be stuck here for at least half a year.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:44.270
If you make any mistakes, it'll be longer.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:47.310
I must leave here because 
there are things I need to do.

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:49.260
So does everyone else.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:54.720
Anyway, now that we're here, 
be careful about Chief Takasu.

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:59.930
It's rumored that he wields his 
authority to do whatever he wants.

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:15.360
He's a Signer?

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:20.620
You heard rumors about the Crimson Dragon.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:23.770
He's a candidate.

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:26.470
But in our examination, he had no mark.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:32.650
Chief, I did not come here 
to hear your opinions.

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:37.170
Make sure you keep your eye on him.

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:39.760
Impossible!

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:42.590
It's not allowed to be true!

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:46.160
That garbage from Satellite 
must not be a Signer!

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:51.600
I'll teach him that garbage 
will always be garbage!

00:05:56.820 --> 00:05:59.070
Do you want to escape?

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:04.830
There's no one here who 
doesn't want to escape.

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:11.660
When they brought you here, I bet they told you 
that you could leave soon.  However, that's a lie.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:18.310
They keep outsiders who come to Domino 
City here in order to set an example.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:23.140
I was also supposed to leave here 
quickly, but it's already been a year.

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:26.930
If you want to escape, want to come with me?

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:36.450
It took half a year.  Do you 
want to see what's up ahead?

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:45.360
Look.

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:50.600
From that opening, we can reach the 
upper portions of Neo Domino City.

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:52.770
But how?

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:56.490
My friends will come to 
rescue me tomorrow night.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:06:59.210
But what about this?

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:02.880
If we leave the detention center, it 
will begin transmitting immediately.

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:07.700
No problem!  My friends will jam the 
security system via the internet.

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:12.050
The marker won't transmit for one hour.

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:14.340
It's a method that can only be used once.

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:17.440
If they discover the jamming, 
the system will be changed

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:20.690
to something new, and that 
hole might also be discovered.

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:22.390
I have one request.

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:27.010
I want to include two 
more people in this plan.

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:29.600
Himuro and that grandpa?

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:34.150
Fine.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:41.480
Anyway, if we don't escape between 8 and 9 
o'clock tomorrow, we won't have a second chance.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:42.880
Got it?

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:52.490
Why won't it appear?

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:08.350
In order to make the Crimson Dragon 
appear, it seems I must duel him again.

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:22.590
What do you want?

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:26.700
I've received information 
that you're hiding weapons.

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:28.460
Weapons?

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:31.880
I don't have any.

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:34.850
Go ahead and search my room.

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:38.730
That's not necessary.

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:42.060
See?  I found one.

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:43.440
How dare you!

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:51.290
What did that new arrival tell you?

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:53.400
What do you mean?

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:59.500
Besides, I never sell out my friends.

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:03.240
That garbage from Satellite is your friend?

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:08.040
The former pro duelist has fallen far.

00:09:29.550 --> 00:09:31.380
Himuro!

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:33.260
Himuro…

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:36.720
Himuro committed a huge crime!

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:40.460
Everyone here will be held responsible!

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:44.160
Your free time is revoked for an entire year!

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:47.490
No one is allowed to leave their cells!

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:48.790
Wait!

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:51.280
That's the same as being in solitary!

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:52.750
That's right!

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:54.080
Be quiet!

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:59.670
Garbage like you has no right to complain!  
You're all worthless in society!

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:04.280
You do not have the right for freedom!

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:09.270
Just continue to live pathetically 
in the shadows for eternity!

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:10.950
If you have any complaints, then speak up!

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:14.530
If you do, you'll end up the same way as him!

00:10:16.710 --> 00:10:17.890
Wait!

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:25.690
No one in the world is worthless.

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:33.200
My my.  The garbage from 
Satellite thinks he's a hero?

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:35.440
Himuro is innocent.

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:40.370
He's a real duelist.  He wouldn't 
conspire to do anything.

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:45.490
You're saying that even though 
you know that I'm also a duelist?

00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:49.630
You're saying he's real but I'm fake?

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:54.370
Fine.

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:59.350
Let's settle things in a 
duel in front of everyone!

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:06.130
If you win, I'll ignore Himuro's crime, and I 
promise not to take away everyone's free time.

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:09.800
However, if I win…

00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:12.340
I'll do whatever you want 
for the rest of my life.

00:11:14.930 --> 00:11:16.520
Interesting.

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:20.820
The duel will take place 
tonight at 8:30.  Understand?

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:22.340
Fine.

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:25.340
Hey, how can you say that when he's…

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:26.660
Stop!

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:29.510
Please stop!

00:11:29.510 --> 00:11:30.970
Keep coming!

00:11:32.310 --> 00:11:33.790
I found one!

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:34.490
And here.

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:35.270
And here.

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:37.050
And here.

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:40.300
Wait!  Those are my treasures!

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:43.010
Give them back!  Please!

00:11:47.710 --> 00:11:50.140
I'm confiscating this deck.

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:55.150
Listen, this will be your final free time!

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:58.130
Spend it well so that you have no regrets!

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:05.900
Yusei, why did you do that?  
We're supposed to escape tonight!

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:08.550
I know.

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:33.730
Himuro.

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:35.210
Yusei.

00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:36.600
Are you okay?

00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:39.060
Sorta.

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:44.780
Yusei,  I'm sorry.  They also took my deck.

00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:50.030
Oh no!  They took my deck.

00:12:50.030 --> 00:12:51.570
Himuro, are you okay?

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:52.550
Himuro!

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:54.250
Himuro!

00:12:54.780 --> 00:12:56.050
Is he okay?

00:12:56.050 --> 00:12:59.810
Understand?  This is how 
the chief does things.

00:12:59.810 --> 00:13:04.030
He never intended to have a 
fair duel from the beginning.

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:07.290
You fell for his taunts.

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:10.160
Himuro and grandpa's decks were confiscated.

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:12.840
Without a deck, you have no chance.

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:17.010
Let's escape, just the two of us.

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:20.060
In their current state, those 
two won't be able to make it.

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:22.240
I can't do that.

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:26.120
Why not?  You don't owe 
these people anything.

00:13:26.230 --> 00:13:29.130
Since we dueled, we're now friends.

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:34.500
If I leave my friends behind, 
I'll never truly be free.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:38.500
Stop acting tough when you have no deck.

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:39.710
Do whatever you want!

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:40.980
Sheesh!

00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:44.750
You said your name was Yusei?

00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:47.640
You were quite the showoff.

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:49.710
Come with us for a minute.

00:13:57.880 --> 00:13:59.380
Come out!

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:02.730
Yusei!

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:04.820
Don't mind me.

00:14:12.090 --> 00:14:17.300
Hero of Satellite, you need a deck to duel.

00:14:17.300 --> 00:14:22.450
You did bring one, right?

00:14:22.450 --> 00:14:27.530
If you don't have one, then 
I win this duel by forfeit!

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:32.370
I have a deck.

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:34.770
Impossible!

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:36.730
From where?

00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:44.490
You will never understand how much 
a duelist cares for a single card.

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:47.320
Come with us for a minute.

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:56.060
A duelist always keeps his 
most special card with him.

00:14:57.570 --> 00:14:59.770
I want you to have this.

00:14:59.770 --> 00:15:06.160
If you didn't oppose him, we would have 
continued to feel pathetic forever.

00:15:08.710 --> 00:15:10.760
You can do it!

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:14.640
Defeat him.

00:15:18.260 --> 00:15:21.720
Please beat him with this!

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:26.060
I'll carry your emotions with me.

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:35.350
Well, fine.

00:15:35.420 --> 00:15:39.120
If you have a deck, then I'll just 
have to squash you in a duel.

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:42.300
You guys!  Hurry up and 
prepare the Duel Disks!

00:15:45.690 --> 00:15:47.530
What's this chain?

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:51.040
It's just for a little show.

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:55.690
Only the survivor gets to 
take off this Duel Disk.

00:15:55.880 --> 00:15:57.890
Only the survivor?

00:15:58.160 --> 00:16:00.440
You'll understand soon enough.

00:16:04.850 --> 00:16:06.140
Duel!

00:16:09.010 --> 00:16:14.640
I refuse to believe that a garbage 
from Satellite is a Signer.

00:16:14.860 --> 00:16:16.320
My turn.

00:16:17.110 --> 00:16:20.460
I summon Great Phantom 
Thief in defense position.

00:16:22.900 --> 00:16:25.960
Hey look!  That's my card!

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:27.620
I end my turn.

00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:29.150
Be careful.

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:33.050
Even though everyone put their 
emotions into that deck,

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:36.530
it's still a random deck 
without strategy or theory.

00:16:36.530 --> 00:16:38.820
But Bro can do it!

00:16:38.820 --> 00:16:40.920
It's my turn.

00:16:41.130 --> 00:16:45.110
I draw!  I summon Iron Chain Repairman!

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:53.940
Iron Chain Repairman attacks your monster!

00:16:54.440 --> 00:16:57.610
Go, Iron Chain Repairman!

00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:05.140
My card…

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:10.030
At this moment, Iron Chain Repairman's 
monster effect activates!

00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:15.290
When it destroys a monster in battle, 
you take 300 points of damage!

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:19.920
Prepare yourself, garbage hero.

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:20.960
What?

00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:26.010
Yusei!

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:27.410
Yusei!

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:36.180
Oh, I'm sorry.  I forgot to explain.

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:40.330
This Duel Disk has a special mechanism.

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:45.360
When you take damage, an equal amount 
of electricity flows through it.

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:46.610
What?

00:17:46.610 --> 00:17:51.750
From past examples, it's unlikely that 
the loser of this duel will live.

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:57.220
That's what I meant when I said that only the 
survivor would be able to remove the Duel Disk.

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:02.480
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:07.140
My turn.

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:11.310
I summon The Kick Man in attack position!

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:14.270
That's my card!

00:18:14.270 --> 00:18:19.030
Go, Yusei!  The Kick Man 
will blast Takasu to bits!

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:23.180
Then the Equip Spell Stim-Pack.

00:18:23.180 --> 00:18:27.860
The equipped monster gains 700 attack points.

00:18:34.290 --> 00:18:37.520
The Kick Man, attack Iron Chain Repairman.

00:18:39.850 --> 00:18:44.030
I won't let you do that!  
Continuous Trap Soul Anchor!

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:48.430
This card is equipped on 
to Iron Chain Repairman.

00:18:48.430 --> 00:18:52.830
When this card is on the field, 
it cannot be destroyed in battle!

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:58.240
However, you still take damage.

00:18:58.940 --> 00:18:59.900
He did it!

00:18:59.900 --> 00:19:02.780
Now he will also receive an electric shock.

00:19:13.470 --> 00:19:15.490
I don't believe it.

00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:20.140
It seems my Duel Disk is malfunctioning.

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:22.170
What?

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:25.040
This is also his trap.

00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:30.880
That's cheating!  There never was electricity 
flowing through his Duel Disk from the beginning!

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:35.020
Stop making false accusations.

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:37.890
It's not my fault that it's malfunctioning.

00:19:37.890 --> 00:19:40.890
You're a cheater!

00:19:43.970 --> 00:19:46.920
Yusei, stop!  This duel doesn't count!

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:48.940
That's not allowed!

00:19:48.940 --> 00:19:55.770
I apologize to your hero, but 
it's no reason to stop the duel.

00:19:55.770 --> 00:19:58.100
The duel will continue!

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:04.050
My turn!

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:07.540
From my hand, I summon Iron Chain Snake!

00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:13.060
Take Iron Chain Snake's monster effect!

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:23.550
Iron Chain Snake is equipped on to your 
monster, and it loses 800 attack and defense points.

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:26.370
Go, Iron Chain Repairman!

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:46.420
When Iron Chain Repairman destroys a monster 
in battle, you take 300 points of damage!

00:20:49.210 --> 00:20:50.170
Yusei!

00:20:50.170 --> 00:20:51.270
Yusei!

00:20:50.170 --> 00:20:51.520
Bro!

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:55.260
That's not all.

00:20:55.260 --> 00:20:59.020
When a monster equipped with Iron 
Chain Snake is destroyed in battle,

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:04.210
its controller has to send cards 
from his deck to the graveyard

00:21:04.210 --> 00:21:07.210
equal to the Level of the equipped monster.

00:21:07.240 --> 00:21:09.370
The Kick Man's Level is three.

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:16.370
Now send three cards from 
your deck to the graveyard!

00:21:24.190 --> 00:21:27.780
I'll soon send you back to that 
garbage dump you call a hometown!

00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:30.610
But I'm going to kill you first!

00:21:32.350 --> 00:21:34.350
Yusei!

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:35.690
Stand up!

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:39.490
Stand up, Yusei!

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:10.460
What can we grasp?  What can we do?

00:22:10.820 --> 00:22:15.850
We'll step forward and find out

00:22:16.230 --> 00:22:21.780
My unstoppable emotions, the 
beating of my passionate heart

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:27.020
I heard the voice of truth

00:22:27.210 --> 00:22:30.180
After I was hurt, I learned

00:22:32.750 --> 00:22:35.770
Of a place where I can become stronger

00:22:37.720 --> 00:22:42.930
I stack my dreams in my palm

00:22:43.060 --> 00:22:48.330
And I'll someday pass them to you

00:22:48.760 --> 00:22:54.270
Seeking for the signal 
to start, my soul roars

00:22:54.570 --> 00:22:59.610
I will overcome my suffocating 
and mediocre life

00:23:00.170 --> 00:23:05.700
I'll dash and acquire all the bright futures

00:23:05.850 --> 00:23:15.120
Carrying the bonds I believe 
in, I run towards tomorrow
